{
  "paraId": "3B67F28A",
  "style": "",
  "text": "Several limitations of this study should be acknowledged. First, although the MIMIC-IV database includes patients from diverse ethnic groups (Asian, White, Black, and Hispanic), the retrospective design and the high severity of illness of the study population may limit the generalizability of our findings. Second, several potentially important confounders, such as socioeconomic and nutritional status, were not collected in the database and may therefore have influenced the observed outcomes. Third, diagnoses were ascertained from ICD codes, which may have introduced misclassification bias. These findings therefore warrant confirmation in other populations, and the mechanisms linking SHR to the prognosis of HF merit further investigation. Future studies should also determine the optimal management of stress hyperglycemia, with the aim of improving survival in patients with HF."
}

